      "category": "ai",
      "title": "Tmux and Claude Code: Sessions, Send-Keys, and the Ceiling",
      "url": "https://crystl.dev/guides/tmux-for-ai-agents/",
      "discuss_url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50148855",
      "score": 145,
      "comments": 107,
      "author": "ankitg12",
      "published": "2026-10-19T05:55:31Z",
      "bullets": [
        "Orchestrating Anthropic's Claude Code via tmux send-keys enables scriptable, asynchronous multi-session agent workflows directly inside terminal environments.",
        "Programmatic CLI automation struggles with non-deterministic output parsing, interactive prompt blocking, and fragile session state management across detached panes.",
        "Terminal multiplexing hits a ceiling for autonomous agents, exposing the need for structured tool-calling APIs over simulated keystroke interfaces."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "lobsters",
      "subsource": "lobste.rs/programming",
      "category": "engineering",
      "title": "In Context",
      "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=P5eO7BNyJao",
      "discuss_url": "https://lobste.rs/s/b36ixw",
      "score": 10,
      "comments": 5,
      "author": "veqq",
      "published": "2026-10-19T18:25:48Z",
      "bullets": [
        "Thread cancellation and request deadlines explicitly through call stacks rather than relying on global state or ambient execution contexts.",
        "Restrict context values strictly to cross-cutting concerns like trace IDs and authentication tokens, avoiding business-logic parameter smuggling.",
        "Treat context termination as non-blocking, ensuring resource cleanup and goroutine termination propagate reliably under high concurrency."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "lobsters",
      "subsource": "lobste.rs/security",
      "category": "security",
      "title": "Tor VPN Beta: What we've learned building our own VPN for Android from scratch",
